            "answer": "<p>Fair question. Pre-orders are what let a one-person company commit to a production run at all — we need to know how many to make before we can make any.</p><p>What you get in return is the launch price and a place in the first run. What you risk is nothing, because you can cancel for a full refund right up until it ships.</p>"
